<section class="agent-control-model" aria-labelledby="agent-control-heading">
  <div class="model-heading" data-reveal>
    <div class="eyebrow">Visibility → Understanding → Control</div>
    <h3 id="agent-control-heading">Discovery is evidence, not authorization.</h3>
    <p>Seeing an agent connected to a system does not prove what it can do. Move from inventory to effective access, then enforce the boundaries.</p>
  </div>
  <ol class="model-stages" role="list">
    <li class="control-stage" data-reveal>
      <span class="stage-label">01 / Find</span>
      <h4>Visibility</h4>
      <p>Find agents, endpoints, OAuth grants and MCP connections. Record the relationships your discovery sources can actually show.</p>
      <strong>What is operating here?</strong>
    </li>
    <li class="control-stage" data-reveal>
      <span class="stage-label">02 / Interpret</span>
      <h4>Understanding</h4>
      <p>Establish business purpose, accountable ownership and human context. Trace credentials, reachable resources and effective permissions.</p>
      <strong>What can it do, and for whom?</strong>
    </li>
    <li class="control-stage featured" data-reveal>
      <span class="stage-label">03 / Govern</span>
      <h4>Control</h4>
      <p>Manage agent identity and least privilege. Enforce policy, approvals and runtime authorization, with monitoring, review and revocation.</p>
      <strong>What should it be allowed to do?</strong>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="model-principle" data-reveal>Keep predictable operations deterministic. Use agentic reasoning where it adds value, with human approval where risk demands it.</p>
</section>

